course: dictionary
lesson: 9568
title: One word, many meanings: strand
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one you need. A strand is a single thin thread, hair or wire, or one part of a story, plan or argument. «Pull one thread and the whole web moves, like a spider's web when one strand is touched.» Here a strand is a thin thread.
explain: Look at the verb in «In 1741 sailors stranded on cold islands in the far north Pacific.» To strand someone means to leave them stuck somewhere with no way to leave. Stranded is the past form, so the sailors were left stuck with no way off the islands.
explain: Strand can also mean a beach or the shore, but this is a literary meaning, so you will meet it mostly in older or poetic books. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have found the right one.
fact: A strand is a single thin thread, hair or wire, or one of several twisted together.
fact: «Kneading lines up gluten proteins into long stretchy strands that trap the gas like balloons.» Here strands are long, thin pieces.
fact: To strand someone means to leave them stuck somewhere with no way to leave; they are stranded.
fact: A strand can also be one part of a story, plan, argument, or school course, such as the number strand in maths.
fact: In the literary sense, a strand is a beach or the shore.
exercise: «Each hair grows from a tiny pocket in the skin called a follicle; the strand you see is dead keratin.» What does strand mean in this sentence? | A sandy beach by the sea | To leave someone stuck | One part of a plan | *A single thin hair
exercise: «In 1741 sailors stranded on cold islands in the far north Pacific saw huge gentle animals.» What does stranded mean here? | Sleeping soundly | Swimming very fast | *Left stuck with no way to leave | Painted in bright colours
exercise: «Our maths course has several strands, such as the number strand.» What does strand mean here? | To leave someone behind | A thin rope of hair | *One part of a course | A stretch of sand
test: «Optical fibres are thin strands of glass that carry light along bends.» What does strand mean in this sentence? | *A thin thread or wire | To leave someone stuck | A beach or the shore | One part of a story
test: «Whales sometimes strand themselves on beaches.» What does strand mean here? | To swim very fast | To dive deep under the sea | To sing loudly as they swim | *To be left stuck on the shore
exam: «The waves rolled up the strand and left shells on the sand.» What does strand mean here? | To leave someone stuck | *A beach or the shore | A thread of wool | A part of a plan
